{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531105-crossover-question","id":1531105,"title":"Crossover question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-19T05:16:02-08:00","id":1531105,"title":"Crossover question","content":"Discussing their ideas for a setting focussing on the area between the \u2018Prairie Provinces\u2019 of Canada and areas of the Northern Great Plains of the USA with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> made me think a bit about what sort of references to other works set in the area one could smuggle into \u2018RAGE ACROSS THE PRAIRIES\u2019 (I\u2019d call this a working title, but it\u2019s more on the order of a convenient handle, not least since this hypothetical work isn\u2019t my own brainchild and I therefore do not claim ownership).<br /> <br /> As this topic touches on the place where Werewolves meet Canada (and Western Canada to boot) my thoughts turned to the man, the myth, the legend THE WOLVERINE (Alias Logan aka \u2018Patch\u2019 formerly James Howlett) rather more quickly than it takes me to types this up (Quite possibly in less time than it takes to read this, even).<br /> <br /> It then occurred to me to ask \u201cIf Logan were one of the Garou, what Auspice and what Tribe would he belong to?\u201d<br /> <br /> Fellow fans, this is the sort of question only a fool would try to answer without throwing the floor open to discussion - after all, there are so many possible answers! - so how would YOU stat up the old Canucklehead as a World of Darkness Werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T14:40:56-08:00","id":1531142,"title":"","content":"My top pick would be a Bone Gnawer Ahroun.<br /> <br /> While there are a lot of options, here are the features that clinch it for me:<br /> <br /> 1) He's very fighty, but also fights with little care for honor or glory. This gruff scrappiness makes him a better fit for the Gnawers than other fighty Tribes like the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> 2) He's a reject from a rich family. Coupled with his memory issues, he effectively has very little connections to his birth family or lineage. Despite having a relatively easy to hide mutation, he also struggles to keep up a normal life even when compared other characters and prefers to eschew polite society for either rough and tumble rural areas, or the bad parts of urban ones. So, like many Gnawers that might have been born to other Tribes, he's happy to not be part of his born family and much prefers his found family instead.<br /> <br /> 3) Related to 1 a bit, Logan has an approach to romance that's very out-of-step with the Garou Nation. While he's generally a very good partner while his relationships last, he's long since given up on &quot;honorable&quot; mating and trying to produce well breed offspring. He find love when he can, and doesn't think it will last (and generally he's right even if it's turned into a bit of self-sabotage). He's had a lot of kids, many of which have inherited some of his powers, but due to his serial monogamy being as rampant as it is, he's far more likely to find out about them when they come knocking on his door for answers about why he's never been around and why he left their mothers to whatever shitty lives (and frequently deaths) when he could have been helping them out.<br /> <br /> 4) He's really good at socializing in marginalized societies. Despite being an aggressive white dude, he generally does better with criminals, the poor, and persecuted minorities (not even getting into mutants) than he does with mainstream society. Though this does tend to make 3 worse as it means a lot of his love interests really needed him to stick around even as just a father figure (something he's actually really good at with kids that aren't his... except Laura and she's a partial clone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T15:26:01-08:00","id":1531145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531105-crossover-question?p=1531142#post1531142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My top pick would be a Bone Gnawer Ahroun.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Iguess he is more like a Ronin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T20:42:37-08:00","id":1531171,"title":"","content":"He's been a member of multiple superhero teams (and whatever you want to call the Weapon X program when they put him to work with other test subjects). He has his problems with how things are run, but he joins up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T19:18:35-08:00","id":1531266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531105-crossover-question?p=1531142#post1531142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My top pick would be a Bone Gnawer Ahroun.<br /> <br /> While there are a lot of options, here are the features that clinch it for me:<br /> <br /> 1) He's very fighty, but also fights with little care for honor or glory. This gruff scrappiness makes him a better fit for the Gnawers than other fighty Tribes like the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> 2) He's a reject from a rich family. Coupled with his memory issues, he effectively has very little connections to his birth family or lineage. Despite having a relatively easy to hide mutation, he also struggles to keep up a normal life even when compared other characters and prefers to eschew polite society for either rough and tumble rural areas, or the bad parts of urban ones. So, like many Gnawers that might have been born to other Tribes, he's happy to not be part of his born family and much prefers his found family instead.<br /> <br /> 3) Related to 1 a bit, Logan has an approach to romance that's very out-of-step with the Garou Nation. While he's generally a very good partner while his relationships last, he's long since given up on &quot;honorable&quot; mating and trying to produce well breed offspring. He find love when he can, and doesn't think it will last (and generally he's right even if it's turned into a bit of self-sabotage). He's had a lot of kids, many of which have inherited some of his powers, but due to his serial monogamy being as rampant as it is, he's far more likely to find out about them when they come knocking on his door for answers about why he's never been around and why he left their mothers to whatever shitty lives (and frequently deaths) when he could have been helping them out.<br /> <br /> 4) He's really good at socializing in marginalized societies. Despite being an aggressive white dude, he generally does better with criminals, the poor, and persecuted minorities (not even getting into mutants) than he does with mainstream society. Though this does tend to make 3 worse as it means a lot of his love interests really needed him to stick around even as just a father figure (something he's actually really good at with kids that aren't his... except Laura and she's a partial clone).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is perfection. I had never seen him so characterised so well.<br /> <br /> Could you care to suggest some stats perhaps?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T21:36:14-08:00","id":1531271,"title":"","content":"Statting up long running characters is always a bit fraught because there's been so many characterizations by so many writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T15:12:59-08:00","id":1531309,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I think your characterisation of Old Man Logan well thought-out: my own notion was, oddly enough, to make him a Glass Walker Ragabash - based on his ability to function in urban society (Though only for a time) and deal with everyday people without leaving every single one of them terrorised, I assumed that his Rage would be relatively low-level (and he\u2019s definitely got the \u2018questioner of the ways\u2019 element down cold, being a natural contrarian and prone to be a pragmatist amongst idealists and a relative idealist amongst cynics).<br /> <br /> I admit to also equating his time with Weapon X to a bad experience with the CyberDogs; in the context of a Glass Walker tribal affiliation, it bears pointing out his sometime association with organised crime dovetails quite neatly with the Wise Guys bailiwick and his time in the Far East makes perfect sense for a tribe with strong connections to the area (Most especially Hong Kong).<br /> <br /> While Logan is unusually fond of time in the wilds for a Glass Walker, it bears pointing out that the northern forests are Logan\u2019s refuge and that he spends most of his career working out of one city or another (and it\u2019s also worth considering that hugs Garou self might be a throwback to the Iron Riders of the Wyld West, who were known to spend a fair bit of time in the Wild Country).<br /> <br /> <br /> To my mind Logan/Wolverine as Glass Walker works very neatly because - on a storytelling level - this would<br /> make him a figure a bit outside the mainstream of his tribe, but an extremely useful go-between when dealing with the rougher elements of modern society (Or, for that matter, the Bone Gnawers and non-Urban Garou), as well as a useful expert to call on for matters military, especially when plotting some wilderness campaign.<br /> <br /> In addition, I place Logan with the Glass Walkers because with the Tribe of Cockroach he stands out as a Roughneck, in his usual style: with the Bone Gnawers he\u2019d just be another one of the guys!\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T00:31:24-08:00","id":1531339,"title":"","content":"Glass Walker Ragabash is certainly a way to go with it, though it is very out of keeping with how the books tend to present the Glass Walker approach to Ragabash.<br /> <br /> While I don't really feel like debating the finer points on why I went the way I did over that, one would point out is that the Bone Gnawers that are very active in Garou Society - esp. to the pint of getting leadership positions in mixed groups - are considered extremely exceptional. Most of the Gnawers stick to their own. The Rabble that makes up most of the true numbers of the Tribe tend to participate just enough to be counted, but otherwise keep their heads down. It's the Rat's Teeth that are the ones that go out and really try to get shit done. Of course, most PCs are Rat's Teeth because playing the Rabble isn't really a good play loop for most people, so it skews what people play alongside how the setting is described. But a Bone Gnawer that has the social success Logan has with the X-Men and other teams would be an exceptional member of the Gnawers if you translated that to things like being a member of a well regarded pack, having a Sept Office, etc. while not being in a Gnawer primary Sept or Protectorate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T06:17:22-08:00","id":1531351,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, you make an excellent series of points - one must admit that I mostly wanted to advance an alternate theory to help encourage other readers to post their own ideas (If on it because, as you mentioned, there are a great many takes on Wolverine in the comics, so there should be plenty of room for multiple interpretations of him in Garou form).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I suspect his WEREWOLF 5th Edition counterpart would almost have to be a Galestalker (Since the tribe\u2019s emphasis on tracking fits quite neatly and the \u2018Best there is at what I do \u2026 what I do ain\u2019t very nice\u2019 energy is strong with them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T15:30:57-08:00","id":1531387,"title":"","content":"I think the W5 changes would certainly sway much stronger in that direction. He also makes a lot of sense as a member of the pre-Cult of Fenris Tribe that opted to join the Glass Walkers instead of the Cult. It helps highlight him as a bit different from the rest of the Tribe, and possibly was a more worldly Garou before losing a lot in the fallout of the Cult's formation that would help make him fit the lower scale take on things that W5 has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T08:32:39-08:00","id":1531517,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s nice to know that even 5th Edition can sometimes make<br /> life easier for a Storyteller!\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:42:12-08:00","id":1531803,"title":"","content":"It does make one wonder how a person defined by slashing murderous technology to bits could ever sruvive the W5 Glass Walker tribal ban,though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:09:37-08:00","id":1531958,"title":"","content":"Thank God for the Galestalkers, then!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}